<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daria Daulat Bagh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1784</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daria Daulat Bagh is the summer palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangapatna">Srirangapatna</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built in 1784 in the Indo-Islamic style and set in a large garden. Its teak walls are covered with painted murals, among them a large scene of the victory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and Tipu over the British at Pollilur in 1780. The palace now houses a museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/daria-daulat-bagh.jpg" alt="Daria Daulat Bagh" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rahulpurushot · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gumbaj_containing_tomb_of_Tipu_Sultan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
